# Git — always use pull requests to `main`

For every change set:

1. Use a **feature branch** (`git checkout -b <branch>` if you are on `main` and need a new branch).
2. Commit when the user asked for commits (or when completing their requested change set).
3. Push the branch: `git push -u origin HEAD` (use `git -c core.hooksPath=.githooks push` in this clone if global hooks block; see [README](../../README.md)).
4. **Do not use the `gh` CLI** for this repository. Open a PR on **github.com** using **git + browser only:** give the maintainer the **Compare** URL so they can click **Create pull request** into `main`:
   `https://github.com/meet7202/womens-health-duo/compare/main...<branch>?expand=1`  
   Replace `<branch>` with the pushed branch name (slashes are fine in the path). Optionally paste a suggested title/body in chat; the human completes the PR on GitHub.

Phrases like **“push these changes”** mean **push the branch** and supply the **compare** (or final PR) link — not `git push origin main`.

Do **not** `git push origin main` or merge to `main` locally unless the user **explicitly** asks to skip the PR for that task (rare; default is always PR).
